Chloe's well aware of
the geography, and

00:15:11.681 --> 00:15:16.730
the sequence of events and
Chloe's timing here is perfect.

00:15:16.731 --> 00:15:19.560
That last statement,
why can't we get a dog?

00:15:19.561 --> 00:15:23.781
Is timed not to get an answer,
cuz this is a war of attrition.

00:15:23.782 --> 00:15:25.650
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; This is something in which

00:15:25.651 --> 00:15:28.260
Chloe doesn't want
the answer now.

00:15:28.261 --> 00:15:29.890
She wants to wear
her mother down

00:15:29.891 --> 00:15:33.600
to the point where eventually
she might just say yes.

00:15:33.601 --> 00:15:36.410
And of course,
it starts off with if, and

00:15:36.411 --> 00:15:39.120
ends up with why can't we?

00:15:39.121 --> 00:15:43.905
And, if you like as an example
of someone being entirely

00:15:43.906 --> 00:15:45.890
irresponsive to a context.

00:15:45.891 --> 00:15:50.336
To a spatial and temporal flow
of a car moving through a city

00:15:50.337 --> 00:15:53.640
and an organization of streets.

00:15:53.641 --> 00:15:56.759
If you like a learning context,
Chloe is the ultimate

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:59.590
incarnation of
intelligence here.

00:15:59.591 --> 00:16:04.136
But what I want to suggest is
that it's not Chloe alone,

00:16:04.137 --> 00:16:05.113
of course.

00:16:05.114 --> 00:16:08.668
It's that car moving
through a set of streets.

00:16:08.669 --> 00:16:12.420
It's Chloe's recognition
of various points

00:16:12.421 --> 00:16:15.660
along that street that
builds up this ability for

00:16:15.661 --> 00:16:19.210
her to reach this crescendo
of why can't we get a dog.

00:16:19.211 --> 00:16:22.310
And know that she's not gonna
get an answer for it yet.

00:16:22.311 --> 00:16:25.600
But the intelligence there is
something that is sort of made

00:16:25.601 --> 00:16:28.240
able through Chloe's
movements through space.

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:34.310
And this is what I
want us to think about

00:16:34.311 --> 00:16:38.700
when we talk about intelligence,
is the conditions that are made

00:16:38.701 --> 00:16:41.490
possible through a set
of interactions.

00:16:41.491 --> 00:16:44.780
Through a set of interactions
between ourselves and

00:16:44.781 --> 00:16:47.740
in physical and temporal space.

00:16:47.741 --> 00:16:51.820
That we live in this sort of
fantasy of imagining that we

00:16:51.821 --> 00:16:56.530
might go from something
like solving Go with AI to

00:16:56.531 --> 00:16:57.920
replicating the brain.

00:16:57.921 --> 00:16:59.910
And yet what we don't
really understand is,

00:16:59.911 --> 00:17:02.980
what are the conditions that
we go with making possible?

00:17:02.981 --> 00:17:06.024
Cuz they're not the same as
what we would use the brain for

00:17:06.025 --> 00:17:07.514
in all possible contexts.

00:17:07.515 --> 00:17:12.055
What are the very conditions
that Go enables us to do?

00:17:12.056 --> 00:17:15.547
In fact, Go is probably one of
those few activities that we act

00:17:15.548 --> 00:17:18.530
more like a machine than
we do like a human.

00:17:18.531 --> 00:17:21.476
So it's not surprising,
in a way,

00:17:21.477 --> 00:17:24.227
that AI can solve
that problem and

00:17:24.228 --> 00:17:29.156
not solve Chloe's problem of
talking like a human in a car.

00:17:29.157 --> 00:17:31.580
I am out of time.

00:17:31.581 --> 00:17:34.450
I was gonna talk through
an example of how this might

00:17:34.451 --> 00:17:36.850
be applied to natural
language processing.

00:17:36.851 --> 00:17:40.709
So if anyone wants to talk more
about something of that context,

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:42.499
please come and see me later.

00:17:45.579 --> 00:17:48.330
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

